body.zh:
只展示会影响当下选择的字段：

> **当前任务**：{人物可执行的目标}
>
> **完成条件**：{可观察的达成标准}
>
> **剩余限制**：{时间、次数或当前不可用条件}
>
> **成功所得**：{与主角目标有关的回报}
>
> **使用代价**：{现在就能理解的后果}
>
> **未解锁信息**：只在“未知”本身会改变策略时保留；否则删掉。

面板出现的判断标准是：读完后，主角是否要重新选择。若只是把读者已经知道的属性重复一遍，可以用一句人物反应代替整页列表。

body.en:
Display only fields that affect the present choice:

> **Current task:** {An objective the character can perform}
>
> **Completion condition:** {An observable standard}
>
> **Remaining limit:** {Time, uses, or a condition currently preventing use}
>
> **Reward:** {Something connected to the protagonist’s goal}
>
> **Cost of use:** {A consequence understandable now}
>
> **Locked information:** Keep this only when the unknown itself changes strategy; otherwise remove it.

Use this test: after reading the panel, must the protagonist choose again? If it merely repeats attributes readers already know, replace the full list with one character reaction.

While cuts, narration placement, and speaking duration are still changing, subtitle in and out points will change with them. If you fine-tune every cue too early, moving one line of narration later can leave mistimed, obstructed, or outdated text behind.

Before detailed layout, confirm that:

- the shot order and main cuts are set;
- the narration text matches the actual recording in use;
- you know which original dialogue remains and which hard subtitles are already embedded;
- the positions of signs, documents, and interfaces the audience must read are marked;
- the delivery canvas and any overlapping titles or corner labels have an actual plan.

When the spoken content changes, update the narration and recording before changing the corresponding subtitle. Editing only the on-screen text does not change what the audience actually hears.

A static sample frame confirms only one moment. During full playback, also check whether:

- subtitles appear before the voice begins or linger too long after it ends;
- an old subtitle remains after a cut into the next scene;
- a moving character, raised hand, or displayed object enters the subtitle region;
- the outline, shadow, or backing stays legible as the image shifts between bright and dark;
- a long line suddenly shrinks to fit, causing the type size to jump across the video;
- source hard subtitles, narration subtitles, and titles occupy the same region at once.

Fix the layer that contains the problem. If the text is too long, remove repeated information first. If the position obstructs the image, adjust the layout for that cue or group of cues. If the timing is wrong, check it against the actual sound. If hard subtitles are already embedded in the source pixels, follow the approved editing plan for the picture or choose another region. Do not use animation or borders to conceal incorrect timing.

Judge reading allowance, sound-leading cuts, and speech across shots against this project’s choices. Do not impose identical speech and cue boundaries on every work. A wording or recording change after layout requires updated text, audio, and timing evidence, followed by review of the new export.

body.zh:
把一场戏压成下面五格。格子是检查工具，正文不必按表格口吻写。

> **民国言情场景卡**
>
> 局势事实：{已经成立、会限制行动的事实}
>
> 关系愿望：{甲想要什么；乙想要什么}
>
> 可用抓手：{婚约/报纸/信件/车票/账册/身份文件中的一个}
>
> 双方行动：{甲实际做什么；乙如何接受、拒绝、核对或提出条件}
>
> 场末状态：{物件归属、公开记录、去向或关系边界实际变成什么}

好场景允许安静结束。只要场末状态比开场更明确，人物可以得到理解、暂缓决定或完成一次普通交接；不必为了“乱世感”临时加追兵。下一场再根据已经留下的记录与承诺推进。

body.en:
Compress the scene into five fields. They are a planning check, not prose that must sound like a form.

> **Romance-in-Republican-era-China scene card**
>
> Situational fact: {an established fact that constrains action}
>
> Relationship need: {what A wants; what B wants}
>
> Carrier: {one engagement notice, paper, letter, ticket, ledger or identity document}
>
> Actions: {what A does; how B accepts, refuses, verifies or sets a condition}
>
> End state: {the actual new custody, public record, destination or boundary}

A strong scene may end quietly. If the end state is clearer than the opening, the characters can reach understanding, defer a decision, or complete an ordinary handoff. Do not add pursuers merely to signal a turbulent period. Continue from the record and promise already created.

body.zh:
> 请用 $story-long-write 只规划一场民国言情场景，先不写整章正文。
>
> 本书已定时代与地点：{填写虚构或已核实的设定}
>
> 开场时已经成立的局势事实：{填写}
>
> 甲的关系愿望与边界：{填写}
>
> 乙的关系愿望与边界：{填写}
>
> 本场唯一主要抓手：{婚约告示/报馆校样/信件/车票/商会账册/其他}
>
> 必须发生：{两到四个动作与回应}
>
> 不能提前成立：{尚未确认的感情、身份、历史事实或结果}
>
> 场末可核状态：{物件归属、公开记录、去向与双方已说清的范围}
>
> 先输出“局势事实—关系愿望—抓手—双方行动—场末状态”五格场景卡，再给一版细纲。不要替角色完成未授权的原谅、婚约解除或私奔；不要为了题材氛围另加危机。

若要继续写正文，再单独点名这一章，并把已经核实的历史资料、本书文风和人物知情范围一并提供。

body.en:
> Use $story-long-write to plan one romance scene set in Republican-era China only; do not draft the full chapter yet.
>
> Established period and place: {fictional or verified setting}
>
> Situational fact already true at the opening: {fill in}
>
> Character A’s relationship need and boundary: {fill in}
>
> Character B’s relationship need and boundary: {fill in}
>
> One main carrier: {engagement notice / newspaper proof / letter / ticket / trade ledger / other}
>
> Required actions: {two to four actions and responses}
>
> Must not become true yet: {unconfirmed love, identity, historical fact or result}
>
> Verifiable end state: {custody, public record, destination and agreed scope}
>
> Output the five-field scene card first, then a scene outline. Do not grant unrequested forgiveness, dissolve an engagement or turn the scene into an elopement. Do not add a crisis merely for period atmosphere.

When ready for prose, request that chapter separately and provide verified research, book voice and character knowledge boundaries.

body.zh:
> 请用 $story-long-write 只规划本章的赘婿逆袭翻盘场景，先不写正文。
>
> 对手本场要拿走的利益：{合同/职位/署名/客户/家庭决定权/其他}
>
> 主角当前被低估的身份：{填写}
>
> 主角暂不公开全部背景的具体理由与限制：{填写}
>
> 本场允许披露的一层身份或能力：{填写}
>
> 可核证据：{文件/记录/专业结果/授权}
>
> 有资格确认的人：{填写}
>
> 伴侣自己的目标、查证动作与决定：{填写}
>
> 本场只解决：{一项眼前事项}
>
> 仍待后文处理：{责任、长期信任、完整身份或其他}
>
> 输出“对手行动—主角限制—证据交付—有权回应—伴侣选择—局部结果”六步细纲。不要让围观者无依据集体改口，不让豪车或称呼替代本场所争事项的证据，不提前判定仍待查的责任。

确认这份细纲后，再点名请求写本章。写完核对每个角色实际看到的证据，避免旁观者提前知道隐藏身份全貌。

body.en:
> Use $story-long-write to plan this chapter's married-in son-in-law (`赘婿`) comeback scene only; do not draft prose yet.
>
> Benefit the opponent is trying to take: {contract / role / credit / client / family authority / other}
>
> Protagonist’s underestimated current role: {fill in}
>
> Specific reason and constraint preventing full disclosure: {fill in}
>
> One layer of identity or ability that may be disclosed: {fill in}
>
> Verifiable evidence: {document / record / professional result / authorization}
>
> Qualified confirmer: {fill in}
>
> Partner’s own goal, verification and decision: {fill in}
>
> Immediate matter resolved here: {one item}
>
> Still open: {responsibility, long-term trust, full identity or other}
>
> Output a six-step outline: opponent action, protagonist constraint, evidence delivery, authorized response, partner choice, local result. Do not make observers change sides without evidence, let a luxury car or honorific replace proof, or decide responsibility that remains under review.

After accepting the outline, request the chapter. Check what each character actually saw so observers do not learn the entire hidden identity early.

The protocol lists ten review dimensions: objective change, action candidates, rule evidence, actors, space, items and abilities, knowledge gaps, pacing and feeling, audiovisual anchors, and evidence and boundaries. They are questions to ask while reading each unit, not a form to fill in for every chapter. Record only evidenced findings that affect player actions, world responses or audiovisual identity; leave no placeholder fields and do not retell the plot.

Three of them decide whether there is anything to play later:

- **Action candidates**: actions a player could repeat with choice, feedback or room for skill, including source-backed orders, commissions and errands;
- **Rule evidence**: triggers, costs, exceptions, counters and observable consequences;
- **Actors**: goals, default behaviour, resources, limits, and what they can order or take on.

For space, record ways in and out, thresholds, landmarks, risks and what can change; for knowledge gaps, who knows, misbelieves, hides or lies, and through what carrier. Hard rules, key character goals, grounds for the player role, turning points and endings, and signature anchors need chapter locations, and inferences must be labelled. When the source language differs from the design language, quote the original, add the translations a decision needs, keep one shared glossary, and do not swap rites or religion for another culture’s near-equivalent label.

The excerpt cannot answer the following. These go into design gaps or a to-check list instead of being filled in on the fly:

- What the letter says, and why Du Qi insists it arrive tonight (L4 and L8 offer only claims);
- Whether the month-long ban is ever enforced, and whether Old Wen returns the token on time (L2 only states the rule; the excerpt ends at L10);
- Whether the other eight gates have exceptions (L1 says only that all are barred);
- Whether the lost message recurs across the book.

When aggregating across the book, cite where a conclusion is first established, how it typically operates, its key counterexamples and its final payoff, so an opening-only pattern does not become a hard rule; check numbers, ability limits, relationships, deaths and endings against the text. With only this excerpt, mark the bible as a partial analysis and list unread chapters as not reviewed. Unless you explicitly limit the adaptation to this chapter, it does not move on to concept design (for choosing a range, see [how much of a novel a game should adapt](https://zenstory.ai/novel-to-game/scope-a-novel-game-adaptation-for-a-small-team)).

After the concept stage selects a passage, the skill runs again to append a `fact | evidence location | boundary type` table for it to the bible, including the clothing, weapons, build and position of every on-screen character, with “not specified in the source” where the text is silent. The excerpt never says what Su He wears, so you cannot give her a straw raincoat and call it the original. Once the bible is complete, [choose gameplay from the source’s repeated actions](https://zenstory.ai/novel-to-game/choose-gameplay).
